Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for your interest in Arizona State University. ASU offers conditional undergraduate admission to international applicants who meet academic requirements but have not met the English language proficiency standards.

You can be fully admitted to your ASU degree program by submitting a TOEFL or IELTS score or by enrolling in the ASU-ESL program (also known as AECP) and completing Advanced Level 2. Learn more by visiting http://esl.asu.edu/.

Although each student is reviewed individually, a majority of students admitted to ASU have a TOEFL score of 71 or higher. If you do not think you meet this criteria, please contact me by phone at {!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}.

If you have any questions, please feel free to contact me.

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

